# FurniGen project context

## Architecture

- **`furnigen-core`**: Wardrobe spec types, validation, panel/BOM-oriented structures, pure geometry. No Three.js inside Rust.
- **`furnigen-wasm`**: Thin `wasm-bindgen` boundary; JSON (or bytes) in, mesh/metadata out. Shares types with core via workspace.
- **`web/`**: React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind; Three.js reads WASM output only.

## Units and layout

- **Canonical units**: millimeters in the spec, Rust core, and JSON on the wire.
- **UI**: May display inches or mm; convert at the boundary; never store imperial as the source of truth.
- **Geometry scope (v1)**: Straight runs only. Reserve schema/extension points for future L/U/45° segments without implementing them yet.

## Exports (roadmap)

After interactive preview: cut list/BOM, 2D panel outlines (e.g. SVG/DXF), 3D mesh export (e.g. glTF). Order is flexible; document dependencies and export sequencing in [`docs/decisions/`](../../docs/decisions/) per [technical-decision-log](technical-decision-log.mdc).

## Licensing

- Project license: **GNU GPL-3.0-or-later** (full text in repo root `LICENSE`; summary boilerplate in `COPYRIGHT`). Prefer dependencies compatible with the GPLv3 distribution you intend. Flag license conflicts when adding crates or npm packages. See `README.md` for dependency compliance expectations and planned CI checks (`cargo-deny`, JS license scan).

## Rule provenance

Themes aligned with [PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules) (e.g. TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind, Vitest, Playwright, conventional commits) and `rules-new/` listings; Rust/WASM and furniture-domain rules are **FurniGen-native**, not copied verbatim.
